<title>CANADA: North Prairie grainbelt faces weekend frost risk.</title>
<headline>North Prairie grainbelt faces weekend frost risk.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's northern Prairie grainbelt on Wednesday was forecast to see a slight to moderate risk of frost this weekend, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>A slight risk of frost was forecast for Alberta's foothills Thursday and Friday mornings, Environment Canada's 10-day frost outlook said.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was forecast for Alberta's Peace River Valley Saturday and Sunday mornings while a slight risk of frost was forecast for the northern Prairie grainbelt.</p>
<p>A slight risk of frost was forecast for Alberta's foothills September 10, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
